    rdfs:label "Seattle Childrens Research Institute; Washington; USA" ;
    NIFRID:synonym "Seattle Children''s Research Institute",
        "Seattle Childrens Research Institute" ;
    definition: "A top five pediatric research center in the nation that brings together the best minds in pediatric research to set new standards of pediatric care and find new cures for childhood diseases. Their goal is that every patient at Seattle Children''s has the opportunity to participate in, or benefit from, their groundbreaking research. The research institute is organized into nine centers, each one specializing in areas like cancer immunotherapy, neuroscience and child health and behavior. The centers are supported by faculty from the Treuman Katz Center for Pediatric Bioethics , the nation''s first pediatric bioethics center." .

