    definition: "The University of California, San Diego, also known as UC San Diego, is public research university located in the La Jolla neighborhood of San Diego, California, in the United States. Established in 1960, UCSD has 6 different campuses." .

SCR:011626 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    oboInOwl:hasDbXref "nlx_82387" ;
    rdfs:label "University of Connecticut School of Pharmacy" ;
    NIFRID:synonym "UConn School of Pharmacy" ;
    definition: "The University of Connecticut School of Pharmacy offers challenging programs of study in pharmacy practice and the pharmaceutical sciences. Our exceptional faculty, groundbreaking research, and innovative graduate and professional programs position the School of Pharmacy as one of the top choices for pharmacy education in the United States. Our professional program, which leads to the Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) and our research-intensive graduate programs in medicinal chemistry, pharmaceutics, and pharmacology/toxicology attract the best and brightest national and international students. The School of Pharmacy''s outstanding academic ranking is one of the reasons why U.S. News and World Reports named UConn the top public University in New England." .

