    rdfs:label "University of Georgia College of Pharmacy; Georgia; USA" ;
    NIFRID:synonym "University of Georgia College of Pharmacy" ;
    NIFRID:abbrev "UGA College of Pharmacy" ;
    definition: "The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy offers the Doctor of Pharmacy professional degree. Based in Athens, Georgia and affiliated with the Georgia Health Sciences University (formerly Medical College of Georgia) in Augusta, the college admits about 145 students a year. The four-year professional program integrates classroom, laboratory and experiential training in a curriculum organized around both human physiology and disease states. The college also offers graduate studies in disciplines associated with pharmacotherapeutic research, clinical work, and administration." .

