    definition: "The College of Pharmacy at The University of Texas at Austin is one of the premier institutions of pharmaceutical education and research in the country. Our college is a national leader in pharmacy education with a curriculum designed to prepare pharmacy graduates for lifelong learning and leadership capabilities as drug therapy managers in the nation&apos;s healthcare system. The pharmacist of the 21st century has significant responsibility for managing drug therapy, counseling patients on proper use of medications, and monitoring drug therapy outcomes." .

