        "Wikidata: Q4355568" ;
    rdfs:label "VINNOVA" ;
    NIFRID:synonym "VINNOVA Sweden''s Innovation Agency" ;
    definition: "Swedish agency whose mission is to promote sustainable growth by improving the conditions for innovation, as well as funding needs-driven research. They promote collaborations between companies, universities, research institutes and the public sector by stimulating a greater use of research, by making long-term investment in strong research and innovation environments and by developing catalytic meeting places. Their activities also focus on strengthening international cooperation." .

