        "Quantitative Biology Center",
        "University of Tübingen" ;
    definition: "Central unit for bioinformatics and omics technologies of University of Tübingen, Medical Faculty and Max Plank for Developmental Biology. Through partnering with on campus core facilities, offers services on full range of omics technologies.  Data generation is complemented by integrated bioinformatics analyses, and all high throughput data is managed centrally." .

